  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch13-07> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch13-07--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch13-07--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on thompson1917-ch13-07: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.36" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.356"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "needs-new-data" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.77"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Adhesion and curvature can be defined, but adult museum morphology cannot discriminate adhesion-induced retardation from primary growth asymmetry. New developmental biomechanical data would be needed." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Map sheath-core adhesion strength and local elongation around developing horn bases, then test whether spatially uneven adhesion predicts subsequent curvature independently of intrinsic growth. Experimental or longitudinal evidence that adhesion asymmetry alone generates the observed spiral would support the claim." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "No known open dataset links local sheath-core adhesion to subsequent horn geometry.", "Intrinsic growth and mechanical retardation produce similar final forms.", "The asserted importance requires comparative or perturbational evidence." .
